summary:
I bring financial and scientific expertise to bear to address challenges faced as promising new technologies are commercialized by early-stage enterprises in the cell-therapy, pharma, medical-devices, diagnostics, science-tools, and health-IT industries.  These perspectives help startups' founders and managers set strategic priorities.  In like fashion, my plain-English reporting contributes to better decisions by potential investors and strategic partners, as they weigh rewards and risks.  Baltimore City County, Maryland, United States 'createdAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'updatedAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.292Z', 'actualAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'sentAtToPAS': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.261Z', 'id': 35716, 'personId': 24815, 'title': 'Senior Principal, New Ventures', 'companyName': 'University of Maryland, Baltimore (UMB)', 'companyId': '455844', 'dateRange': 'start': 'year': 2021, 'month': 9, 'end': None, 'locationName': 'Baltimore, Maryland, United States', 'description': "I am UMB's senior Site Miner for TEDCO's Maryland Innovation Initiative, which provides faculty with funding and tools to explore the prospects of commercializing their innovations.  In that role, I work closely with investigators (and startup companies) to design programs to quickly and cheaply answer the key questions for a Go/No-Go decision -- ranging from technology to product/market fit.  I also support the initiatives of New Ventures program, fostering biotech and Health-IT innovation within the UMB community.", 'isDefault': True, 'url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/455844/', 'organizationDescription': None, 'website': None, 'domain': None, 'createdAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'updatedAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.292Z', 'actualAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'sentAtToPAS': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.261Z', 'id': 35717, 'personId': 24815, 'title': 'Business Development Consultant', 'companyName': 'Astek Diagnostics', 'companyId': '85825805', 'dateRange': 'start': 'year': 2021, 'month': 1, 'end': None, 'locationName': 'Baltimore, Maryland, United States', 'description': 'Engage with potential partners and investors as Astek develops diagnostic applications of its innovative rapid metabolism-based tools for assessing bacterial presence and activity.', 'isDefault': False, 'url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/85825805/', 'organizationDescription': None, 'website': None, 'domain': None, 'createdAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'updatedAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.292Z', 'actualAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'sentAtToPAS': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.261Z', 'id': 35718, 'personId': 24815, 'title': 'Independent Consultant', 'companyName': 'Alastair Mackay Consulting', 'companyId': None, 'dateRange': 'start': 'year': 2016, 'month': 4, 'end': None, 'locationName': 'Baltimore, Maryland', 'description': 'Life sciences startups must present their vision and mission to potential investors, clearly and concisely.  I assess these companies' prospects, including:
- Technological innovations and the underlying intellectual property;
- The size and nature of the relevant addressable markets;
- Management's experience and resourcefulness in planning and implementing development;
- Regulatory, pricing, and reimbursement considerations; 
- Prospects for product adoption by end users.  

These elements influence the timing and size of a liquidity event, and thus the present value of an enterprise.  I report on these factors to interested institutional investors and potential strategic partners.  I guide founders and managers in developing product development plans, multiple-year financial projections, and presentations.  

As a 'Site Miner,' I work with entrepreneurial faculty at the University of Maryland, Baltimore to create strong applications to the Maryland Innovation Initiative. These are a great way to explore a technology's readiness for commercialization. I've helped sixteen 'Technology Assessment' and three 'Company Formation' ideas reach "funded" status, along with one MSCRF (stem cell) and one DoD proposal.', 'isDefault': False, 'url': None, 'organizationDescription': None, 'website': None, 'domain': None, 'createdAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'updatedAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.292Z', 'actualAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'sentAtToPAS': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.261Z', 'id': 35719, 'personId': 24815, 'title': 'CEO', 'companyName': 'TrAMPoline Pharma', 'companyId': None, 'dateRange': 'start': 'year': 2020, 'month': 2, 'end': 'year': 2021, 'month': 4, 'locationName': 'Aurora, Colorado, United States', 'description': "TrAMPoline's mission is to advance an autologous T-cell-based immunotherapy for the treatment of recurrent/relapsed solid tumors.", 'isDefault': False, 'url': None, 'organizationDescription': None, 'website': None, 'domain': None, 'createdAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'updatedAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.292Z', 'actualAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'sentAtToPAS': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.261Z', 'id': 35720, 'personId': 24815, 'title': 'CEO', 'companyName': 'Kosmo Technologies, Inc.', 'companyId': '15267672', 'dateRange': 'start': 'year': 2017, 'month': 5, 'end': 'year': 2019, 'month': 7, 'locationName': 'Greater Salt Lake City Area', 'description': 'Medical-device startup Kosmo Technologies worked to develop a fast, accurate, and cheap test of upper airway resistance, to improve the care of patients with Obstructive Sleep Apnea (OSA). The "Airway Optimizer" could be used by dentists to simplify Oral Appliance (OA) therapy, an emerging alternative to Positive Airway Pressure (PAP or CPAP) ventilation. At the first visit, the dentist would use this non-invasive breath test to determine the OA settings that best open the airway for a night of restful sleep, supplanting the "titration" procedure that is currently required. Beyond this dental market, we foresaw applications for the Airway Optimizer in OSA screening, and monitoring respiratory patients.', 'isDefault': False, 'url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/15267672/', 'organizationDescription': None, 'website': None, 'domain': None, 'createdAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'updatedAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.292Z', 'actualAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'sentAtToPAS': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.261Z', 'id': 35721, 'personId': 24815, 'title': 'Senior Life Sciences Principal at the Maryland Venture Fund', 'companyName': 'TEDCO', 'companyId': '6657652', 'dateRange': 'start': 'year': 2015, 'month': 11, 'end': 'year': 2016, 'month': 4, 'locationName': 'Columbia, Maryland', 'description': "The Maryland Venture Fund is the State of Maryland's public-sector venture fund.  As the MVF's Life Sciences Principal at the Dept. of Commerce (2013-2015) and at TEDCO (2015-2016), I evaluated startups and small private companies seeking equity for product development and expansion at the Seed and Series A stages.  I championed the most promising opportunities for the MVF, conducting extensive scientific and financial due diligence, negotiating deal terms, and authoring investment documents.  

Over three years, I was responsible for investing $4.1 million in nine companies (including six follow-on Bridge, Series A, and Series B placements).  By 2020, exits had yielded about $9.4 million for the MVF (~$5.3 million above return of principal). The notable successes were Harpoon Medical (acquired by Edwards Lifesciences in 2017) and Graybug Vision (IPO in 2020).

I held the MVF's Observer seat on the Boards of numerous portfolio companies, helping them to set and achieve key milestones.  To fulfill the MVF's economic development mission, I advised Maryland entrepreneurs on their plans, and helped tune their presentations for external audiences.", 'isDefault': False, 'url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/6657652/', 'organizationDescription': None, 'website': None, 'domain': None, 'createdAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'updatedAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.292Z', 'actualAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'sentAtToPAS': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.261Z', 'id': 35722, 'personId': 24815, 'title': 'Senior Life Sciences Principal at the Maryland Venture Fund', 'companyName': 'TEDCO', 'companyId': '6657652', 'dateRange': 'start': 'year': 2013, 'month': 4, 'end': 'year': 2015, 'month': 10, 'locationName': 'Baltimore, Maryland', 'description': "As the MVF's Life Sciences Principal, I evaluated startups and small private companies seeking equity funding.  In pursuing opportunities with prospects for venture-scale returns, I conducted extensive due diligence and shepherded companies through the investment process. I served as the Fund's Board Observer at numerous portfolio companies.

The reforms proposed by the Augustine Commission led to the transfer of the MVF to TEDCO in mid-2015.", 'isDefault': False, 'url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/6657652/', 'organizationDescription': None, 'website': None, 'domain': None, 'createdAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'updatedAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.292Z', 'actualAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'sentAtToPAS': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.261Z', 'id': 35723, 'personId': 24815, 'title': 'Independent Consultant', 'companyName': 'self-employed', 'companyId': None, 'dateRange': 'start': 'year': 2012, 'month': 9, 'end': 'year': 2013, 'month': 3, 'locationName': 'Baltimore, Maryland Area', 'description': 'Provided insight on addressable markets for science-tool, diagnostic, and medical-device technologies.  Advised startups on the merits of commercialization strategies.', 'isDefault': False, 'url': None, 'organizationDescription': None, 'website': None, 'domain': None, 'createdAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'updatedAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.292Z', 'actualAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'sentAtToPAS': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.261Z', 'id': 35724, 'personId': 24815, 'title': 'Equities Analyst', 'companyName': 'GARP Research & Securities', 'companyId': '143319', 'dateRange': 'start': 'year': 2005, 'month': 2, 'end': 'year': 2012, 'month': 8, 'locationName': 'Reisterstown, MD', 'description': 'As a sell-side analyst, I initiated coverage on select small-cap and mid-cap companies in the diagnostic, medical-device, pharmaceutical, and science-tools sectors.  A combination of quantitative and qualitative tools were employed to project stock performance over a three-year time horizon, based on the "Growth At a Reasonable Price" paradigm.  I kept GARP's institutional clients abreast of developments at covered companies through a mix of written reports and high-touch contact.  

My performance was recognized by Financial Times/Starmine awards in 2009 (#2 in Healthcare Equipment & Supplies; #1 in Life Science Tools & Services), and by the Wall Street Journal’s “Best on the Street” in 2008 (#2 in Medical Equipment & Supplies) and 2007 (#1 in Life Science Tools & Services).', 'isDefault': False, 'url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/143319/', 'organizationDescription': None, 'website': None, 'domain': None, 'createdAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'updatedAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.292Z', 'actualAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'sentAtToPAS': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.261Z', 'id': 35725, 'personId': 24815, 'title': 'Senior Manager & Asst. Director, Cell Biology Program', 'companyName': 'Osiris Therapeutics', 'companyId': '49990', 'dateRange': 'start': 'year': 2002, 'month': 4, 'end': 'year': 2005, 'month': 1, 'locationName': 'Baltimore, MD', 'description': 'Supervised research in mesenchymal stem cell therapy by two staff scientists; managed three major grants from DARPA and NIST.  Was the Principal Investigator of DARPA’s "Metabolic Stasis of MSCs" project.  Authored Standard Operating Procedures in support of Osiris' Investigational New Drug application for the Prochymal cell-therapy product. ', 'isDefault': False, 'url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/49990/', 'organizationDescription': None, 'website': None, 'domain': None, 'createdAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'updatedAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.292Z', 'actualAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'sentAtToPAS': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.261Z', 'id': 35726, 'personId': 24815, 'title': 'Manager, Stromal Biology Program', 'companyName': 'Osiris Therapeutics', 'companyId': '49990', 'dateRange': 'start': 'year': 1999, 'month': 7, 'end': 'year': 2002, 'month': 3, 'locationName': 'Baltimore, MD', 'description': 'Led three-person team that investigated how MSCs support the production of blood cells in the bone marrow. Guided the development of a quantitative RT-PCR potency assay in order to reduce lot-to-lot variability of Prochymal product. Co-authored successful applications for several research grants; coordinated sponsored research at four universities.', 'isDefault': False, 'url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/49990/', 'organizationDescription': None, 'website': None, 'domain': None, 'createdAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'updatedAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.292Z', 'actualAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'sentAtToPAS': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.261Z', 'id': 35727, 'personId': 24815, 'title': 'Senior Research Scientist', 'companyName': 'Osiris Therapeutics', 'companyId': '49990', 'dateRange': 'start': 'year': 1996, 'month': 1, 'end': 'year': 1999, 'month': 6, 'locationName': 'Baltimore, Maryland', 'description': "I devised differentiation assays to assess Mesenchymal Stem Cells' capacity to differentiate into cartilage and muscle, in order to further development of cell-based therapies for connective tissues.  I also served as founding chair of Osiris’ animal experimentation oversight committee (IACUC). ", 'isDefault': False, 'url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/49990/', 'organizationDescription': None, 'website': None, 'domain': None, 'createdAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'updatedAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.292Z', 'actualAt': '2024-03-31T04:22:42.806Z', 'sentAtToPAS': '2024-03-31T04:22:43.261Z', 'id': 35728, 'personId': 24815, 'title': 'Postdoctoral Research Fellow', 'companyName': 'Johns Hopkins University', 'companyId': '3528', 'dateRange': 'start': 'year': 1989, 'month': 3, 'end': 'year': 1996, 'month': 1, 'locationName': 'Baltimore, MD', 'description': "In mentor William Earnshaw's lab, I cloned the INCENP gene.  Designed, carried out, and published experiments proving that the proper expression and localization of this protein is required for the successful completion of cell division.", 'isDefault': False, 'url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/3528/', 'organizationDescription': None, 'website': None, 'domain': None Senior Principal, New Ventures University of Maryland University of Maryland, Baltimore (UMB)

