President PJ Fitzpatrick Executive Advisory Group, LLC PJ Fitzpatrick Executive Advisory Group Highly diverse entrepreneurial & executive leadership background in the medical device, healthcare, consulting & hospitality services arenas.  I have been honored and fortunate to have led teams taking innovated services and technologies from ideation through to commercialization and exit.  My experience includes 10+ start-ups, distressed turnarounds, roll-ups, integration of acquired companies, multi-site & international operations.  Specific industry sectors include: EMS/ambulance advanced life support emergency medical services, physical therapy and rehabilitation services, international nurse recruiting & staffing, breast cancer risk screening, complex Point of Care molecular DX testing and endovascular catheter-based drug delivery medical devices.  Ventures range from pre-revenue to $250M revenue, completing over $50 million of private and venture backed financings and over 20 M&A transactions with a combined value in excess of $100 million.  I provide fractional C-level and board engagements along with advisory services to startups, small companies and truly enjoy serving as a volunteer board member, pro bono mentor to startups and early stage companies along with being a member of several professional industry associations.  I am a graduate of the Northeastern University degree paramedic program, was an adjunct faculty in the paramedic program for 8 years along with being a former Nationally Registered Paramedic, AHA ACLS Provider/Instructor and Massachusetts Paramedic Examiner.    Core Skills & Attributes: Highly passionate about ventures that make a difference in peoples lives Can do, never give up philosophy Believe in the team, building consensus to make good decisions Energetic & strong communicator Start-up, Early Stage Ventures Strategic Planning Executive Leadership Business Development Mergers, Acquisitions, Strategic Alliances Fund Raising P&L & cash flow 